kel.desc:
[no-namespace] allow namespace imports for specific modules
I want to disallow using namespaces as a rule, but some third-party libraries don't use default exports. The specific one that we use quite a bit in our application is [yup](https://github.com/jquense/yup). Even if we use TypeScript's `allowSyntheticDefaultImports` rule, we still have to import the library using `import * as yup from 'yup';`.

I'd like to be able to do something like the following:
```
rules: {
    // ...
    'import/no-namespace': ['warn', {allow: ['yup', 'some-lib', '@scoped/lib']}],
    // ...
},
```

Wi

